menu "sys_lvgl"

    config SYS_LVGL_HEAP_DEFAULT
        int "LVGL's pool at INSTALL (B)"
        default 65536
        range 32768 4194304
        help
          LVGL's one pool when INSTALL gives 0: every object, style and
          cache of the screen. Taken whole at INSTALL, freed at RESET.

    config SYS_LVGL_POOL_RESERVE
        int "Pool reserve (B)"
        default 8192
        range 2048 65536
        help
          What sys_lvgl_pool_check keeps free in LVGL's pool for what LVGL
          allocates by itself while it draws (layers, label lines). A widget
          that would eat into it is refused (ERR_LVGL_POOL_FULL).

    config SYS_LVGL_BUFFER_MAX
        int "Largest draw buffer (B)"
        default 32768
        range 1024 262144
        help
          One draw buffer at most (two are made). Also limited by the
          display's largest FLUSH (GEOMETRY flush_max).

    config SYS_LVGL_FLUSH_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "FLUSH limit (ms)"
        default 200
        range 20 5000
        help
          The longest wait for the end of a FLUSH; past it the adapter reports
          ERR_DISPLAY_FLUSH_TIMEOUT and resets the display.

    config SYS_LVGL_HEALTH_MS
        int "Display check period (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 0 60000
        help
          How often the adapter reads its display's HEALTH while it draws
          (a display whose SDO is wired, SYS_DISPLAY_FLAG_READABLE): no
          answer is reported once (ERR_DISPLAY_LOST) and the screen redrawn
          when it answers again; a panel that lost its power is reset and
          redrawn. 0: never.

    config SYS_LVGL_TASK_STACK
        int "LVGL task stack (B)"
        default 8192
        range 4096 32768

    config SYS_LVGL_TASK_PRIO
        int "LVGL task priority"
        default 4
        range 1 20

endmenu
